# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

This resource allows you to manage a GitHub Actions policy (workflow execution protection) for a repository. Actions policies restrict which events and actors can trigger workflows, optionally scoped to specific workflow files. You must have admin access to the repository to use this resource.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/actions_repository_policy/example_1.tf" }}

## Argument Reference

The following arguments are supported:

- `repository` - (Required) The name of the repository. Changing this forces a new resource.
- `name` - (Required) The name of the policy.
- `enforcement` - (Required) The enforcement level of the policy. Can be one of `disabled`, `active`, or `evaluate`. `evaluate` is only available with GitHub Enterprise.
- `workflow_path` - (Optional) Restrict the policy to matching workflow files. If omitted, the policy applies to all workflows. See [Workflow Path](#workflow-path) below for details.
- `allowed_events` - (Optional) The events that are allowed to trigger matching workflows, for example `pull_request` or `pull_request_target`.
- `allowed_actor` - (Optional) The actors that are allowed to trigger matching workflows. Can be specified multiple times. See [Allowed Actor](#allowed-actor) below for details.

### Workflow Path

- `include` - (Optional) Workflow file paths or glob patterns to include. An empty list includes all workflows not matched by `exclude`.
- `exclude` - (Optional) Workflow file paths or glob patterns to exclude.

### Allowed Actor

- `id` - (Required) The ID of the actor.
- `type` - (Required) The type of the actor. Can be one of `User`, `Bot`, `Team`, `BusinessTeam`, `EnterpriseTeam`, `IntegrationInstallation`, `App`, or `RepositoryRole`.

## Attributes Reference

- `policy_id` - The ID of the policy.

## Import

This resource can be imported using the repository name and policy ID, separated by a colon:

```shell
terraform import github_actions_repository_policy.example my-repository:123
```
